</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Dataset statistics: number of documents in each dataset split (#Train/Val/Test), average number of words (i.e., Avg. W) and mentions (i.e., Avg. M) per document.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> To gauge the effectiveness of our methods, we follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martinelli et al. (2024)</a></cite> by adopting DeBERTa<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{large}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>large</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{large}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al. (2021)</a></cite> as the base model for ImCoref.
Meanwhile, we choose three latest and most robust LLMs for ImCoref-CeS: Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team (2024)</a></cite>, DeepSeek-R1-250528 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI (2025)</a></cite> and GPT-4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a></cite>. For clarity, we denote ImCoref-CeS with different LLMs as <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ImCoref-CeS<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{qwen/dpsk/gpt4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">qwen/dpsk/gpt4</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{qwen/dpsk/gpt4}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.
Also, we compare ImCoref-CeS and ImCoref against numerous baselines: 1) <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Supervised neural methods</span> including c2f-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Joshi et al. (2020)</a></cite>, ICoref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xia et al. (2020)</a></cite>, CorefQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2020)</a></cite>, s2e-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirstain et al. (2021)</a></cite>, longdoc <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Toshniwal et al. (2021)</a></cite>, wl-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dobrovolskii (2021)</a></cite>, f-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Otmazgin et al. (2022a)</a></cite>, LingMess <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Otmazgin et al. (2022b)</a></cite>, Dual-cache <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. (2023)</a></cite>, and Maverick<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{mes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>mes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{mes}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martinelli et al. (2024)</a></cite>; 2) <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Generative methods</span> containing ASP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2022)</a></cite>, Link-Append <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bohnet et al. (2023)</a></cite>, and seq2seq <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2023)</a></cite>; 3) <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Large Language Models</span> comprising InstructGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a></cite>, GPT-3.5-turbo <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, GPT-4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a></cite>, and LLMLink <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
Notably, for fairness, our methods align with the text encoding strategy of Maverick<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{mes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>mes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{mes}}</annotation></semantics></math> in comparative experiments, without considering the LBM module. The utility of LBM will be thoroughly investigated in the ablation study.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:672.8pt;height:386.5pt;vertical-align:-190.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(30.4pt,-17.5pt) scale(1.09950608945364,1.09950608945364) ;">
<table id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Methods</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Base Encoders</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text">MUC</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text">B<sup id="S4.T2.2.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_sup">3</sup></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text">CEAF<math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\phi_{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\phi_{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
