<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention</span>: Refers to a specific occurrence in the text of one or more consecutive words used to refer to an entity (person/object/place/organization/concept, etc.), including pronouns, noun phrases, or descriptive spans. A mention must be a sequence of consecutive words, and usually does not include irrelevant punctuation (such as periods, question marks, or commas), unless the punctuation is an integral part of the entity’s name (e.g., “U.S.A.”).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coreference Task</span>: Group mentions at different positions in the text that point to the same entity into one cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Numbering Format</span>: Each mention is assigned a unique number in the format “#X”, where X is a numeral (e.g., “#1: you” indicates that the mention “you” is numbered #1).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Annotation Format in Text</span>: In text with numbered mentions, the start of each mention is marked with “[(#X)” and the end with “](#X)” (where X is a numeral), with no space between the markers and adjacent words (e.g., “[(#1)you](#1)” represents the mention “you” numbered #1). This ensures the location of each mention instance is unique, avoiding confusion between mentions with the same form.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Checking Criteria
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Determine “Yes”</span>: When all mentions clearly refer to the same entity in context.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Determine “No”</span>: When at least one mention in the cluster clearly refers to a different entity.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Determine “Pending”</span>: When the context does not allow confirmation of coreference relationships for all mentions.
