<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T10.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:690.0pt;height:940.7pt;vertical-align:-468.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-103.0pt,140.4pt) scale(0.770102439824975,0.770102439824975) ;">
<table id="A3.T10.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T10.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:880.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Your task is to regroup a coreference cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Task Description
<br class="ltx_break">- Input includes: A original text, a coreference cluster result (with a set of numbered mentions), and text with these numbered mentions marked.
<br class="ltx_break">- Your task is: The input coreference cluster has been identified as incorrect (not all mentions point to the same entity). You need to regroup these mentions based on the text context, ensuring each new group’s mentions refer to the same entity, and different groups’ mentions refer to different entities. The output must include the reasons for regrouping and the regrouping results.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Key Definitions
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention</span>: Refers to a specific occurrence in the text of one or more consecutive words used to refer to an entity (person/object/place/organization/concept, etc.), including pronouns, noun phrases, or descriptive spans. A mention must be a sequence of consecutive words, and usually does not include irrelevant punctuation (such as periods, question marks, or commas), unless the punctuation is an integral part of the entity’s name (e.g., “U.S.A.”).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coreference Task</span>: Group mentions at different positions in the text that point to the same entity into one cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Numbering Format</span>: Each mention is assigned a unique number in the format“#X”, where X is a numeral (e.g., “#1: you” indicates that the mention “you” is numbered #1).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Annotation Format in Text</span>: In text with numbered mentions, the start of each mention is marked with “[(#X)” and the end with “](#X)” (where X is a numeral), with no space between the markers and adjacent words (e.g., “[(#1)you](#1)” represents the mention “you” numbered #1). This ensures the location of each mention instance is unique, avoiding confusion between mentions with the same form.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Annotation Method</span>: All mentions in the input are marked in the above format. Only these numbered mentions can be used for grouping. Unmarked parts of the text only provide context.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Regrouping Criteria
<br class="ltx_break">Strictly follow these rules for regrouping:
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intra-group Consistency</span>: All mentions in a new group must clearly refer to the same entity.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inter-group Exclusivity</span>: Mentions in different groups must refer to different entities.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completeness</span>: The regrouping must include all mentions from the original cluster without omission.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conflict Resolution</span>: If a mention’s affiliation is unclear, place it in a new group.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scope Limitation</span>: Only process mentions in the input cluster; do not introduce other unmarked mentions from the text.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Nested Mention Handling</span>: For nested mentions (one mention containing another), determine their affiliation based on context: group them together if they refer to the same entity, otherwise separate them.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T10.2.1.1.1.1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Failure Handling</span>: If correction is impossible (e.g., insufficient context or ambiguous mention reference), return the reason for failure. Otherwise, output the reasons and results.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Output Format Requirements
<br class="ltx_break">- First, provide a brief analysis (within 100 words) of the original cluster’s error and the regrouping basis.
<br class="ltx_break">- Then, output the regrouped mention numbers. The format is comma-separated groups, each group expressed as: [#list of numbers] (e.g., [#1,#2,#4], [#3,#5]). Numbers must be in ascending order and only from the original cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">- The output must end with the grouping result, with no extra content or explanation.
<br class="ltx_break">- Example output structure: “Reason text. [#1, …], [#X, ..], …”.
<br class="ltx_break">- If correction fails, output “Correction failed:” followed by the reason (e.g., “Correction failed: Insufficient context to determine the entity reference of #3”), then end the output.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T10.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="A3.T10.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T10.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:880.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<span id="A3.T10.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">### Input to be Regrouped
<br class="ltx_break">
Original text: 
<br class="ltx_break">
The government sold the deposits of four savings - and - loan institutions , in its first wave of sales of big , sick thrifts , but low bids prevented the sale of a fifth . The four S&amp;Ls were sold to large banks , as was the case with most of the 28 previous transactions initiated by the Resolution Trust Corp. since it was created in the S&amp;L bailout legislation two months ago . Two of the four big thrifts were sold to NCNB Corp. , Charlotte , N.C. , which has aggressively expanded its markets , particularly in Texas and Florida . A Canadian bank bought another thrift , in the first RTC transaction with a foreign bank . Under these deals , the RTC sells just the deposits and the healthy assets . These “ clean - bank ” transactions leave the bulk of bad assets , mostly real estate , with the government , to be sold later . In these four , for instance , the RTC is stuck with $ 4.51 billion in bad assets . Acquirers paid premiums ranging from 1.5 % to 3.7 % for the deposits and branch systems , roughly in line with what analysts were expecting . The buyers will also be locked into deposit rates for just two weeks , as has been the case with previous deals . After that , the buyers may repudiate the rates paid by the former thrifts .

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">
Coreference cluster result (with a set of numbered mentions): 
<br class="ltx_break">
#1:The government, #2:four savings - and - loan institutions, #3:its, #4:The four S&amp;Ls, #5:the four big thrifts, #6:the government, #7:these four, #8:the former thrifts

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">
Text with these numbered mentions: 
<br class="ltx_break">
[(#1)The government](#1) sold the deposits of [(#2)four savings - and - loan institutions](#2) , in [(#3)its](#3) first wave of sales of big , sick thrifts , but low bids prevented the sale of a fifth . [(#4)The four S&amp;Ls](#4) were sold to large banks , as was the case with most of the 28 previous transactions initiated by the Resolution Trust Corp. since it was created in the S&amp;L bailout legislation two months ago . Two of [(#5)the four big thrifts](#5) were sold to NCNB Corp. , Charlotte , N.C. , which has aggressively expanded its markets , particularly in Texas and Florida . A Canadian bank bought another thrift , in the first RTC transaction with a foreign bank . Under these deals , the RTC sells just the deposits and the healthy assets . These “ clean - bank ” transactions leave the bulk of bad assets , mostly real estate , with [(#6)the government](#6) , to be sold later . In [(#7)these four](#7) , for instance , the RTC is stuck with $ 4.51 billion in bad assets . The buyers will also be locked into deposit rates for just two weeks , as has been the case with previous deals . After that , the buyers may repudiate the rates paid by [(#8)the former thrifts](#8) .</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T10.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A3.T10.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:880.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T10.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">LLM Output:
<br class="ltx_break">
The original cluster incorrectly grouped government mentions with thrifts/S&amp;Ls. “The government” (#1,#3,#6) refers to the governing entity managing the RTC, while “four savings-and-loan institutions” (#2), “The four S&amp;Ls” (#4), “the four big thrifts” (#5), “these four” (#7), and “the former thrifts” (#8) all reference the same four financial institutions involved in the sales. These entities are distinct and must be separated. [#1,#3,#6], [#2,#4,#5,#7,#8]</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Example 3 of LLM coreference Checker-Splitter with the incorrect coreference cluster (<span id="A3.T10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">coreference corrector</span>).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T11" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T11.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:690.0pt;height:878.1pt;vertical-align:-436.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-40.2pt,51.1pt) scale(0.895714815436933,0.895714815436933) ;">
<table id="A3.T11.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T11.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:755.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Your task is to check whether all mentions in a coreference cluster point to the same entity.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Task Description
<br class="ltx_break">- Input includes: A original text, a coreference cluster result (with a set of numbered mentions), and text with these numbered mentions marked.
<br class="ltx_break">- Your task is: To determine if all mentions in the cluster clearly point to the same entity. If all mentions point to the same entity, output “Yes”; if at least one mention points to a different entity, output “No”; if there is insufficient information to determine, output “Pending”.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Key Definitions
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention</span>: Refers to a specific occurrence in the text of one or more consecutive words used to refer to an entity (person/object/place/organization/concept, etc.), including pronouns, noun phrases, or descriptive spans. A mention must be a sequence of consecutive words, and usually does not include irrelevant punctuation (such as periods, question marks, or commas), unless the punctuation is an integral part of the entity’s name (e.g., “U.S.A.”).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coreference Task</span>: Group mentions at different positions in the text that point to the same entity into one cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Numbering Format</span>: Each mention is assigned a unique number in the format “#X”, where X is a numeral (e.g., “#1: you” indicates that the mention “you” is numbered #1).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Annotation Format in Text</span>: In text with numbered mentions, the start of each mention is marked with “[(#X)” and the end with “](#X)” (where X is a numeral), with no space between the markers and adjacent words (e.g., “[(#1)you](#1)” represents the mention “you” numbered #1). This ensures the location of each mention instance is unique, avoiding confusion between mentions with the same form.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Checking Criteria
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Determine “Yes”</span>: When all mentions clearly refer to the same entity in context.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Determine “No”</span>: When at least one mention in the cluster clearly refers to a different entity.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Determine “Pending”</span>: When the context does not allow confirmation of coreference relationships for all mentions.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Output Format Requirements
<br class="ltx_break">- First, output the reason for the judgment (a brief analysis within 50 words).
<br class="ltx_break">- Then, output the judgment result, which must be: “Yes”, “No”, or “Pending”.
<br class="ltx_break">- The output should end with the judgment result, with no extra content or explanation.
<br class="ltx_break">- Example output structure: “Reason text. Yes”, “Reason text. No”, or “Reason text. Pending”</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T11.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T11.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T11.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="A3.T11.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:755.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<span id="A3.T11.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">### Input to be Checked
<br class="ltx_break">
Original text: 
<br class="ltx_break">
SOUTH AFRICA FREED the ANC ’s Sisulu and seven other political prisoners . Thousands of supporters , many brandishing flags of the outlawed African National Congress , gave the anti-apartheid activists a tumultuous reception upon their return to black townships across the country . Most of those freed had spent at least 25 years in prison . The 77 - year - old Sisulu , sentenced to life in 1964 along with black nationalist Nelson Mandela for plotting to overthrow the government , said equality for blacks in South Africa was in reach . The releases , announced last week by President de Klerk , were viewed as Pretoria ’s tacit legalization of the ANC . Mandela , considered the most prominent leader of the ANC , remains in prison .

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">
Coreference cluster result (with a set of numbered mentions): 
<br class="ltx_break">
#1:SOUTH AFRICA, #2:FREED, #3:the ANC ’s, , #4:the outlawed African National Congress, #5:the country, #6:the government, #7:South Africa, #8:The releases , announced last week by President de Klerk ,, #9:Pretoria ’s, #10:the ANC, #11:the ANC

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">
Text with these numbered mentions: 
<br class="ltx_break">
[(#1)SOUTH AFRICA](#1) [(#2)FREED](#2) [(#3)the ANC ’s](#3) Sisulu and seven other political prisoners . Thousands of supporters , many brandishing flags of [(#4)the outlawed African National Congress](#4) , gave the anti-apartheid activists a tumultuous reception upon their return to black townships across [(#5)the country](#5) . Most of those freed had spent at least 25 years in prison . The 77 - year - old Sisulu , sentenced to life in 1964 along with black nationalist Nelson Mandela for plotting to overthrow [(#6)the government](#6) , said equality for blacks in [(#7)South Africa](#7) was in reach . [(#8)The releases , announced last week by President de Klerk ,](#8) were viewed as [(#9)Pretoria ’s](#9) tacit legalization of [(#10)the ANC](#10) . Mandela , considered the most prominent leader of [(#11)the ANC](#11) , remains in prison .</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T11.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T11.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A3.T11.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:755.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T11.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">LLM Output:
<br class="ltx_break">
The cluster includes mentions of South Africa (country) and the ANC (organization), which are distinct entities. Mentions like #1 (SOUTH AFRICA), #5 (the country), #7 (South Africa), and #9 (Pretoria’s, referring to South Africa’s government) point to the country. Mentions #3 (the ANC’s), #4 (the African National Congress), #10, and #11 refer to the ANC. These are different entities.
No</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
