</figure>
<figure id="A3.T12" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T12.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:690.0pt;height:922.2pt;vertical-align:-459.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-103.0pt,137.7pt) scale(0.770102439824975,0.770102439824975) ;">
<table id="A3.T12.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T12.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:880.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Your task is to regroup a coreference cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Task Description
<br class="ltx_break">- Input includes: A original text, a coreference cluster result (with a set of numbered mentions), and text with these numbered mentions marked.
<br class="ltx_break">- Your task is: The input coreference cluster has been identified as incorrect (not all mentions point to the same entity). You need to regroup these mentions based on the text context, ensuring each new group’s mentions refer to the same entity, and different groups’ mentions refer to different entities. The output must include the reasons for regrouping and the regrouping results.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Key Definitions
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention</span>: Refers to a specific occurrence in the text of one or more consecutive words used to refer to an entity (person/object/place/organization/concept, etc.), including pronouns, noun phrases, or descriptive spans. A mention must be a sequence of consecutive words, and usually does not include irrelevant punctuation (such as periods, question marks, or commas), unless the punctuation is an integral part of the entity’s name (e.g., “U.S.A.”).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coreference Task</span>: Group mentions at different positions in the text that point to the same entity into one cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Numbering Format</span>: Each mention is assigned a unique number in the format“#X”, where X is a numeral (e.g., “#1: you” indicates that the mention “you” is numbered #1).
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Annotation Format in Text</span>: In text with numbered mentions, the start of each mention is marked with “[(#X)” and the end with “](#X)” (where X is a numeral), with no space between the markers and adjacent words (e.g., “[(#1)you](#1)” represents the mention “you” numbered #1). This ensures the location of each mention instance is unique, avoiding confusion between mentions with the same form.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mention Annotation Method</span>: All mentions in the input are marked in the above format. Only these numbered mentions can be used for grouping. Unmarked parts of the text only provide context.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Regrouping Criteria
<br class="ltx_break">Strictly follow these rules for regrouping:
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intra-group Consistency</span>: All mentions in a new group must clearly refer to the same entity.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inter-group Exclusivity</span>: Mentions in different groups must refer to different entities.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completeness</span>: The regrouping must include all mentions from the original cluster without omission.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conflict Resolution</span>: If a mention’s affiliation is unclear, place it in a new group.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scope Limitation</span>: Only process mentions in the input cluster; do not introduce other unmarked mentions from the text.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Nested Mention Handling</span>: For nested mentions (one mention containing another), determine their affiliation based on context: group them together if they refer to the same entity, otherwise separate them.
<br class="ltx_break">- <span id="A3.T12.2.1.1.1.1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Failure Handling</span>: If correction is impossible (e.g., insufficient context or ambiguous mention reference), return the reason for failure. Otherwise, output the reasons and results.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">### Output Format Requirements
<br class="ltx_break">- First, provide a brief analysis (within 100 words) of the original cluster’s error and the regrouping basis.
<br class="ltx_break">- Then, output the regrouped mention numbers. The format is comma-separated groups, each group expressed as: [#list of numbers] (e.g., [#1,#2,#4], [#3,#5]). Numbers must be in ascending order and only from the original cluster.
<br class="ltx_break">- The output must end with the grouping result, with no extra content or explanation.
<br class="ltx_break">- Example output structure: “Reason text. [#1, …], [#X, ..], …”.
<br class="ltx_break">- If correction fails, output “Correction failed:” followed by the reason (e.g., “Correction failed: Insufficient context to determine the entity reference of #3”), then end the output.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T12.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T12.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="A3.T12.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:880.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<span id="A3.T12.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">### Input to be Regrouped
<br class="ltx_break">
Original text: 
<br class="ltx_break">
SOUTH AFRICA FREED the ANC ’s Sisulu and seven other political prisoners . Thousands of supporters , many brandishing flags of the outlawed African National Congress , gave the anti-apartheid activists a tumultuous reception upon their return to black townships across the country . Most of those freed had spent at least 25 years in prison . The 77 - year - old Sisulu , sentenced to life in 1964 along with black nationalist Nelson Mandela for plotting to overthrow the government , said equality for blacks in South Africa was in reach . The releases , announced last week by President de Klerk , were viewed as Pretoria ’s tacit legalization of the ANC . Mandela , considered the most prominent leader of the ANC , remains in prison .

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">
Coreference cluster result (with a set of numbered mentions): 
<br class="ltx_break">
#1:SOUTH AFRICA, #2:FREED, #3:the ANC ’s, , #4:the outlawed African National Congress, #5:the country, #6:the government, #7:South Africa, #8:The releases , announced last week by President de Klerk ,, #9:Pretoria ’s, #10:the ANC, #11:the ANC

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">
Text with these numbered mentions: 
<br class="ltx_break">
[(#1)SOUTH AFRICA](#1) [(#2)FREED](#2) [(#3)the ANC ’s](#3) Sisulu and seven other political prisoners . Thousands of supporters , many brandishing flags of [(#4)the outlawed African National Congress](#4) , gave the anti-apartheid activists a tumultuous reception upon their return to black townships across [(#5)the country](#5) . Most of those freed had spent at least 25 years in prison . The 77 - year - old Sisulu , sentenced to life in 1964 along with black nationalist Nelson Mandela for plotting to overthrow [(#6)the government](#6) , said equality for blacks in [(#7)South Africa](#7) was in reach . [(#8)The releases , announced last week by President de Klerk ,](#8) were viewed as [(#9)Pretoria ’s](#9) tacit legalization of [(#10)the ANC](#10) . Mandela , considered the most prominent leader of [(#11)the ANC](#11) , remains in prison .</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T12.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A3.T12.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:880.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T12.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">LLM Output:
<br class="ltx_break">
The original cluster incorrectly groups distinct entities: country (South Africa), organization (ANC), government (Pretoria), and non-entity actions/events (FREED, releases). Regrouping based on entity consistency:
- Mentions #1 (SOUTH AFRICA), #5 (the country), #7 (South Africa) refer to the nation.
- #3 (the ANC’s), #4 (the outlawed African National Congress), #10 (the ANC), #11 (the ANC) refer to the ANC organization.
- #6 (the government) and #9 (Pretoria’s) refer to the governing authority.
- #2 (FREED) is an action, not an entity.
- #8 (The releases…) describes an event, not a coreferring entity.
[#1,#5,#6,#7,#9], [#2,#8], [#3,#4,#10,#11]</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
