<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span>Dataset statistics: number of documents in each dataset split (#Train/Val/Test), average number of words (i.e., Avg. W) and mentions (i.e., Avg. M) per document.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> To gauge the effectiveness of our methods, we follow  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martinelli et al. (2024)</a></cite> by adopting DeBERTa<math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{large}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>large</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{large}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al. (2021)</a></cite> as the base model for ImCoref.
Meanwhile, we choose three latest and most robust LLMs for ImCoref-CeS: Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team (2024)</a></cite>, DeepSeek-R1-250528 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI (2025)</a></cite> and GPT-4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a></cite>. For clarity, we denote ImCoref-CeS with different LLMs as <span id="A5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ImCoref-CeS<math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{qwen/dpsk/gpt4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">qwen/dpsk/gpt4</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{qwen/dpsk/gpt4}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.
Also, we compare ImCoref-CeS and ImCoref against numerous baselines: 1) <span id="A5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Supervised neural methods</span> including c2f-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Joshi et al. (2020)</a></cite>, ICoref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xia et al. (2020)</a></cite>, CorefQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2020)</a></cite>, s2e-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirstain et al. (2021)</a></cite>, longdoc <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Toshniwal et al. (2021)</a></cite>, wl-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dobrovolskii (2021)</a></cite>, f-coref <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Otmazgin et al. (2022a)</a></cite>, LingMess <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Otmazgin et al. (2022b)</a></cite>, Dual-cache <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. (2023)</a></cite>, Maverick<math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{mes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>mes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{mes}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martinelli et al. (2024)</a></cite>; 2) <span id="A5.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generative methods</span> containing ASP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2022)</a></cite>, Link-Append <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bohnet et al. (2023)</a></cite>, seq2seq <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2023)</a></cite>; 3) <span id="A5.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Large Language Models</span> comprising InstructGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a></cite>, GPT-3.5-turbo <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, GPT-4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Le and Ritter (2023)</a></cite> and LLMLink <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
Notably, for fairness, our methods align with the text encoding strategy of Maverick<math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{mes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>mes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{mes}}</annotation></semantics></math> in comparative experiments, without considering the LBM module. The utility of LBM will be thoroughly investigated in the ablation study.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics.</span>
In our experiments, coreference performance across different methods is evaluated using the MUC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vilain et al. (1995)</a></cite>, B<sup id="A5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_sup">3</sup> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bagga and Baldwin (1998)</a></cite>, and CEAF<math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\phi_{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\phi_{4}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo (2005)</a></cite> metrics, with Precision (P), Recall (R), and F1 scores reported for each. The overall performance of a method is measured by the CoNLL-F1 score, computed as the average of the F1 scores from these three metrics (abbreviated as Avg.F1). To further analyze model capabilities, certain ablation studies also report Precision (P), Recall (R), and F1 scores for Mention Detection.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Configurations.</span>
In all experiments, unless otherwise specified, we default to setting <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{max}}=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{max}}=30</annotation></semantics></math> for HyMR, <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}=\eta_{2}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}=\eta_{2}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1e-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1e-3</annotation></semantics></math>. Meanwhile, we employ the Adafactor optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shazeer and Stern (2018)</a></cite> for model training, setting the learning rate for the DeBERTa<math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{large}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>large</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{large}}</annotation></semantics></math> to 2e-5 and for the remaining model layers to 3e-4.
All experiments are implemented using the PyTorch-Lightning framework. Each run is executed on a single RTX 4090 GPU with 24GB of VRAM. We have eight such GPUs available, allowing multiple experiments to be conducted concurrently. For fairness, neither data nor model parallelism is employed in any experiment.
During training, we accumulate gradients every four steps and set the gradient clipping threshold at <math id="A5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. A linear learning rate scheduler is adopted, incorporating a warm-up phase covering <math id="A5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> of all training steps. To monitor performance, a validation evaluation is performed every one epoch. The final model is selected based on Avg.F1 in the validation set, with an early stopping patience of <math id="A5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math>. For the LLMs utilized, we access them remotely via their API interfaces, uniformly setting the temperature parameter to <math id="A5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we report additional experimental results, as detailed in Tables <a href="#A6.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ ImCoref-CeS: An Improved Lightweight Pipeline for Coreference Resolution with LLM-based Checker-Splitter Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>-<a href="#A6.T20" title="Table 20 ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ ImCoref-CeS: An Improved Lightweight Pipeline for Coreference Resolution with LLM-based Checker-Splitter Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>. Meanwhile, we utilize ImCoref-CeS<math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{gpt4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>gpt4</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{gpt4}}</annotation></semantics></math> to report the performance across different <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> values on OntoNotes and LitBank, as shown in Fig. <a href="#A6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ ImCoref-CeS: An Improved Lightweight Pipeline for Coreference Resolution with LLM-based Checker-Splitter Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T15" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A6.T15.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:690.0pt;height:458.9pt;vertical-align:-226.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(81.0pt,-53.9pt) scale(1.30668204946841,1.30668204946841) ;">
<table id="A6.T15.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A6.T15.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="A6.T15.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Methods</span></td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="A6.T15.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Base Encoders</span></td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" colspan="3">MUC</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" colspan="3">B<sup id="A6.T15.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_sup">3</sup></td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" colspan="3">CEAF<math id="A6.T15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\phi_{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\phi_{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="A6.T15.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Avg.F1</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T15.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">P</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">R</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">F1</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">P</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">R</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">F1</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">P</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">R</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.2.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">F1</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T15.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" colspan="12"><span id="A6.T15.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Supervised neural methods</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T15.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">c2f-coref</td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r">SpanBERT<math id="A6.T15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{large}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>large</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{large}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T15.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">85.8</td>
